          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with the batteries you own, then compare watt-hours, not voltage badges. For a fresh start on a typical lot, the EGO ST1623T is the strongest all-round battery string trimmer, with the most energy in its kit and the easiest head to live with. Milwaukee M18 owners should take the QUIK-LOK kit, Ryobi ONE+ owners the P20190, and Makita LXT owners the light XRU23.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Match the line size to the growth you cut, buy an attachment system only if you will use a second attachment, and if your lot takes more than one charge, buy a second battery rather than a bigger trimmer. That is how a cordless trimmer ends up as the tool you actually reach for.
